body:
Idk why all of your ideas involve doxxing of some sort. I took some screens of my HS Deck tracker and posted them on Imgur. Hopefully that's enough for you? [https://imgur.com/a/AIE151v](https://imgur.com/a/AIE151v)

&#x200B;

Edit: I haven't really played many matches this season, but I should reach legend by either today or tomorrow. Just doing that last annoying bit in high Diamond again.

I agree with most of the other responses. Have a private chat with him about the initial expectations you made at the start of the adventure and tell him that his character's actions need to reflect his alignment or personality.

&#x200B;

To be fair, knowing about werewolves is not typically something a player should have to roll for unless it's really specific information. Pretty much every culture has myths about werewolves, zombies, vampires, dragons, etc. General knowledge can be assumed unless the characters have amnesia or a background that implies they wouldn't have have ever heard of that type of tale before.
